\paragraph{Comprehensive validation ($n{=}36$).}
Evaluating on the primary experimental conditions yields $n{=}36$, spanning Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, and key ablation configurations. At the $2.0\times$ threshold: AUROC${=}1.000$, precision${=}1.000$, recall${=}1.000$, F1${=}1.000$, accuracy${=}36/36$. Zero false positives: all non-CIVO NVE transients (frozen embeddings, endpoint dips) remain below $2.0\times$. All CIVO-positive configurations are correctly detected (FN${=}0$), with CIVO-positive NVE ranging from $2.09\times$ (008d seed~3, late-onset) to $70.64\times$ (010b seed~0, Cheetah). The $2.0\times$ threshold achieves perfect separation between mechanistic CIVO and non-CIVO transients.

\paragraph{Experiment composition.}
The $n{=}36$ set comprises 9~CIVO-positive and 27~non-CIVO configurations across two environments: Walker Walk (29) and Cheetah Run (7). CIVO-positive experiments include the primary factorial collapse seeds (008d~s1/s4, 059~s5, 006), two pre-correction 008e\_v3 seeds (s2, s3; see below), and cross-environment validation (010b, 010b\_s0, 021). Non-CIVO experiments span all control conditions: removed embedding (008f, 4~seeds), unexposed embedding (008a, 5~seeds), frozen embedding (015b, 022b, 042, 047, 057, 046), baseline (001~s1), and three configurations relabeled from CIVO to non-CIVO under the revised sustained-CIVO classification (009b~s2, NVE~$1.62\times$; 008d~s3, NVE~$1.53\times$; 018~s1, NVE~$1.66\times$), which exhibit transient NVE elevation without the sustained positive-feedback loop characteristic of CIVO. This extends the original $n{=}17$ analysis (Tables~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b1}--\ref{tab:sensitivity_b2_full}) by 19~configurations spanning additional seeds, frozen controls, and cross-environment replications, without changing the AUROC or optimal threshold. The $\tau{=}2.0\times$ threshold was selected on the $n{=}17$ set and maintained unchanged through the $n{=}36$ extension; the clean separation gap (lowest CIVO $2.09\times$ vs.\ highest non-CIVO $1.88\times$) confirms that the threshold generalizes without retuning.

\paragraph{Code-version note.}
Two CIVO-positive entries in the $n{=}36$ set---008e\_v3~s2 (NVE~$3.78\times$) and 008e\_v3~s3 (NVE~$4.02\times$)---use pre-correction data (Appendix~\ref{sec:code_corrections}). Under the corrected codebase, s2 exhibits NVE~$0.50\times$ (non-CIVO); s3 was not re-run. Removing these two entries ($n{=}34$, 7~CIVO-positive) or relabeling s2 as non-CIVO does not affect the diagnostic: the lowest remaining CIVO-positive NVE ($4.12\times$, 008d~s1) far exceeds $\tau{=}2.0\times$, and the separation from the highest non-CIVO NVE ($1.88\times$, exp\_057) widens. AUROC${=}1.000$ holds under either code version.

